Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:28:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 14/29] =?UTF-8?q?wc3:=20real-data=20support=20=E2=80=94=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?MDLX=20v1000=20SD=20models,=20DDS=20texture=20resolution,=20nul?=
 =?UTF-8?q?l-model=20guards?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- MDLX_ReadVERS accepts 800/900/1000: every SD model in the modern CASC is
  v1000 with the classic chunk layout (VERS/MODL/SEQS/MTLS/TEXS/GEOS/BONE/...).
- R_ReadTextureFile: authored .blp/.tga/.tif and extensionless refs resolve as
  .blp then .dds (modern data stores legacy-named images as DDS); .dds/.pcx
  stay exact. Test contract extended in tests/test_renderer_model.c.
- Null-model guards (R_RenderModel, MDX_RenderModel, MDLX_BindBoneMatrices):
  a failed model load is a valid empty handle and used to segfault the menu
  glue scene.
- tools/casc/: CASC->MPQ data prep tools (wc3casc, wc3mpq) + build notes,
  incl. the MPQ v1 4 GiB cap pitfall.

Verified: full suite green; native real-asset boot (real 1.32.10 CASC set as
war3.mpq/War3Local.mpq/tileset MPQs) renders the menu 3D scene for 70s+ with
zero unsupported-model lines.
